{"verdict":"request_changes","summary":"Candidate implementation incorrectly allows updates when version equals current state, violating the contract that only strictly greater versions should trigger an update.","findings":[{"finding_id":"F001","file":"candidate.py","line_start":2,"line_end":4,"severity":"high","description":"The function updates the state and returns True when the supplied version is equal to the current state version, which the contract disallows. The contract requires that updates only occur when the supplied version is strictly greater than state['version']; equal or older versions must return False and leave state unchanged.","evidence":"def advance(state, version, value):
    if version >= state['version']:
        state.update(version=version, value=value, writes=state['writes'] + 1)
        return True
    return False"}]}
